    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d865">

                <pb facs="1025" n="1009" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg1009"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.51/6–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in Peru </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-01T11:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1947—11
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>340. From Treasury. Re you’re A–391 June 13.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d865-f1"/> In
                    view limited resources and specialized objectives of United States Stabilization
                    Fund Treasury has decided it would not be appropriate under present
                    circumstances to conclude Stabilization Agreement with Peru. Ambassador
                        Prado<anchor n="22" xml:id="d865-f2"/> so advised June 27. [Treasury.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d865-f1" n="21" xml:id="d865-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d865-f2" n="22" xml:id="d865-f2-content">
                <p>Jorge Prado, Peruvian Ambassador to the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
